MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Frankie Valli & The 4 Seasons feels like a natural next choice because my mid-'60s and greatest-hits listening points toward familiar older pop songs.",
    "Duets appeals because I enjoyed Cheek to Cheek, while 25 connects with my interest in melodic pop vocals shown by Born This Way."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The country albums feel less connected to the classic pop and folk favorites I want now; being another music album or hits collection is not enough to make me choose one.",
    "16 Biggest Hits and The Best ...So Far sound promising as collections, but without knowing the artists I cannot connect them to songs I enjoy. All That Echoes also has less immediate appeal than the familiar oldies collection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been extended too broadly across artists, even though the songs and performers matter more than the collection format.",
    "My interest in vocal pop seems to have been treated as a broad willingness to try singers, when I am selective about which voices and musical connections appeal right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Repeated choices such as AM Gold: The Mid-'60s, Simon & Garfunkel, and classic rock collections make familiar older songs a particularly strong draw for me.",
    "My interest in newer pop and vocal collaborations sits alongside that older-song preference; it does not mean I am equally interested in exploring country albums."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in hits and vocal music, but stretched those preferences beyond the familiar older pop and specific vocal connections that make me choose an album."
}
